        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thank for taking time and looking at source code! You stopped one step too early, though :) `vim.api.nvim_buf_set_extmakr()` also allows `hl_group` in `virt_text` to set different highlight groups for different parts of text. That is what 'mini.indentscope' is doing via its own two dedicated highlight groups for symbol and what comes before it (prefix):\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/09d70a2cd763c368af749840bcb2a441ea10f971/lua/mini/indentscope.lua#L875-L880\r\n\r\nThe preferred way of managing highlight groups is do redefine you the way you like. [Here is a list](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/09d70a2cd763c368af749840bcb2a441ea10f971/lua/mini/indentscope.lua#L44-L48) of highlight groups of 'mini.indentscope'. So in your case putting the `vim.cmd('hi! link MiniIndentscopeSymbol Whitespace')` somewhere in the 'init.lua' should solve the issue.",
